      "content": "Yes, besides nutrient deficiencies, there are other factors that can contribute to stunted growth and thin patches. Soil issues, such as compacted or poorly draining soil, can limit root growth and impede nutrient uptake. Others include excessive competition from weeds, pests like grub larvae, or even diseases like powdery mildew or leaf spot. Additionally, overwatering, drought, or extreme temperatures can also impact grass health.",
